A||N||7||triksterut||88 GT - Power Steering?||||5||
Z||000000||triksterut||09-13-2000||12:38 PM||||Hey guys,<P>I have an 88 GT I just put 17x7" rims and tires on...steering is now an issue :)  I also just ordered Rodney's Tru-Line steering damper for my 88.  I have heard rumors of a power steering mod for the 88 GT?  It was supposed to ship with some sort of Electro Hydraulic power steering, but I'm pretty sure it doesn't :)  I hear the power steering motor from a Saturn will do it?  Has anyone done any research on this particular project?<P>Jeremy<BR>88 GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||09-13-2000||12:53 PM||||No Fieros ever came from the factory with power steering. It was in the works but was canceled before it could become reality. There is a power steering available but I do not know who does it or any other particulars. It was used in the Zimmerman Quicksilvers. It was mounted over or around the water pump pully. <P>With proper inflation you shouldn't have much of a problem steering or at least not enough to go through the whole hassle of installing it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||triksterut||09-13-2000||01:07 PM||||I mainly wanted to put it on because it would be cool :)  It's just one of those things.  Most of the other stuff is just rationalization which I freely admit :)<P>Jeremy<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000003||HugGRRRFiero||09-13-2000||01:39 PM||||Power steering would have been a cool option on the '89's.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">   I imagine you might run into someone who's put a power steering unit on in here, but I haven't seen a Fiero with one yet.<P>I notice I have far better arm and upper body strength ever since I got mine.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> or maybe it's from all the wrenching I do on it.  Anyway, doesn't really bother me unless I'm driving below 55mph, "you know it gets hard to steer."  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">   <BR>   <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||09-13-2000||06:15 PM||||I was thinking about using the power steering parts from an MR2.  I heard this could be accomplished, but so far I have yet to find an MR2 owner selling the parts.  The saturn one he is reffering to is from the EV1 electric Saturn.  I heard it has a similarly designed electro-hydraulic setup.  I also know Rodney Dickman has an original fiero power steering assembley intended for the later model '88s.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000005||Black88GT||09-13-2000||06:16 PM||||oh yeah as a point of interest, the power steering setup is pictured in the '88 service manual.||||reg||1
Z||000006||rockcrawl||09-13-2000||08:09 PM||||I don't think Rodney's power steering is a system designed for the fiero, nor was it made by GM. From what I remember from previous posts, his and others are using a rack from a Merkur xR4. The pump is engine driven and hydraulic lines run front to rear. <P>With the horrible scrub radius that is part of the fiero's design, power steering would be quite helpful especially with wider tires or offset rims (kit car). 12v electric/hydraulic pumps are readily available, but they are not small nor light. I haven't seen the one used in the EV1. Personally I think it would be far easier to mount a Chevette type (small, remote reservior) pump on the engine and run the lines. <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
Z||000007||Rodney||09-13-2000||10:48 PM||||I have 2 power steering set ups. The power steering in my 88 Mera is the aftermarket Merkur one from the Zimmer. 12.5:1 and nasty nice! Just enough power assist to make it like easy manual steering. I really like it and it makes my Mera a joy to drive. It has the pump on the motor and hoses to the front. <P>I also have an original production 88 power steering rack never installed in an 88. Possibly the only one to survive the crusher from GM. I seen one at the Detroit show. It was a prototype for testing. It had some welding done on it and some temporary parts installed and was used. I do not have the pump though. ||||reg||1
